# WORKFLOW.md — {{ project_name }}

## Branching (Gitflow-lite)

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `main` | Stable / release |
| `{{ default_integration_branch }}` | Integration branch |
| `feat/*`, `fix/*`, `docs/*`, `chore/*` | Temporary work branches |

## Practices

1. Branch off `{{ default_integration_branch }}` for work.  
2. Small PRs / merges; conventional commits.  
3. Temporary branches are ideally **local** until ready to integrate.  
4. Do not force-push shared integration branches without agreement.  

## Delivery

- Product code: `products/` or `services/` with package-level tests when present  
- Host changes: PR to the relevant `hosts/<name>/` tree; apply via that project's control plane  
- Docs: `docs/` with clear area (architecture, ops, product, research)  

## AI-assisted work

- Bounded monorepo jobs: neo-harness (`./scripts/neo`) when embedded  
- Open design: free-form agents with LAYOUT/AGENTS loaded  
